.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
experiments/
# `experiments/` above is a lowercase scratch path. The tracked evidence directory is
# `EXPERIMENTS/`, which differs only by case, so on a case-insensitive filesystem
# (`core.ignorecase=true`, i.e. Windows) that line also matched it and a new evidence
# record written by `scripts/*.py` could not be committed on the maintainer's own machine --
# silently: `git status` simply did not list it. The negation below re-includes the
# directory itself. Re-including a file *inside* an excluded directory would not work;
# re-including the directory does.
!EXPERIMENTS/
data/
checkpoints/
*.pt
.env
*.log
probe*.json
sweep_*.html
probe*.html
